{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1787114437,"nonce":"tm/WTTQZuvhvsw4HHOLT5xQMIwY=","title":"A thread is never frozen: `channel_threads.state` documents a `frozen` that nothing writes, and `Freeze` has no production caller","was":"**What is wrong.** `channel_threads.state` is documented as `opening | open | frozen | dead`, and `00011:197` says what `frozen` means: *\"frozen means the group closed\"*. Nothing ever writes it. `ThreadRepository.Freeze` exists, is declared on the service port, and has **no production caller** — so a thread stays `open` forever after its group closes, and one of the four states the column admits is unreachable in a running deployment."}]}